WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-GB

00:00:00.060 --> 00:00:02.600
Hi guys! This is Kee from BBC Learning English.

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:04.870
Today, I'm going to tell you the differences

00:00:04.870 --> 00:00:08.140
between mustn't and don't have to.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.180
Now, must and have to are similar in meaning.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:14.180
They are both used to describe obligations.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:16.060
However, their negative forms

00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:18.140
are completely different in meaning.

00:00:18.140 --> 00:00:21.260
We still use mustn't to talk about obligations.

00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.240
For example:

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.860
In the house, I mustn't wear shoes.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:26.589
You know, to keep the house clean.

00:00:26.589 --> 00:00:29.920
But don't have to does not describe obligations,

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.620
so the choice is yours!

00:00:32.620 --> 00:00:35.120
For example, if your teacher said:

00:00:35.120 --> 00:00:37.020
you don't have to do your homework,

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:38.800
well... then choice is yours.

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.860
You can say:

00:00:39.860 --> 00:00:41.340
Alright, I won't!

